Package: marble-device-support
Architecture: arm64
# dpkg-shlibdeps runs on the Ubuntu 24.04 build baseline, so the real library
# floors (glibc, GLib, libqmi, libqrtr, libgcc) come from the built binaries
# instead of hand-maintained guesses. The non-library dependencies remain
# explicit because they are data/service assets, not ELF dependencies.
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
 alsa-ucm-conf,
 bluez,
 util-linux (>= 2.34),
 qbootctl,
 qcom-phone-utils,
 modemmanager,
Recommends: 81voltd,
Description: Hardware support layer for Xiaomi Poco F5 (marble)
 Distribution-agnostic hardware support layer for the Xiaomi Poco F5 /
 Redmi Note 12 Turbo (marble, Qualcomm Snapdragon 7+ Gen 2 / SM7475):
 .
  * ALSA UCM2 audio profiles (AW88263S speakers, WCD9385 microphones)
  * udev rules (UFS scheduler, GPU devfreq floor, SSC sensor tagging)
  * systemd services: marble-touchboost, marble-compositor-boost,
    marble-hardware-tuning, marble-panel-on, marble-mac-restore (restores the
    factory WLAN MAC from the persist partition before ath11k loads, and
    programs the factory-derived Bluetooth address, without which the WCN6855
    stays unconfigured and invisible to bluetoothd)
  * marble-ims-enable.service + marble-imsctl: enables the modem's IMS services
    (SMS over IMS, VoLTE) through QMI IMSS, which is what makes SMS and calls
    work on operators without a CS domain. Needs 81voltd, the IMS Data/IMSD
    service the modem asks for the IMS PDN on, hence the Recommends.
  * modprobe blacklist for ath11k_pci, which marble-mac-restore.service loads
    after the MAC file is in place
  * systemd drop-ins for hexagonrpcd and iio-sensor-proxy, retargeted from the
   Alpine/pmOS hexagonrpcd-sdsp.service to Debian's hexagonrpcd.service
  * qbootctl dependency and a drop-in that waits for boot_a/boot_b before
    marking the Linux A/B slot successful, preventing ABL from draining the
    retry counter and falling back to fastboot
  * sysctl (zram dirty-page tuning) and environment.d (GTK4/Wayland)
 .
 This package targets mainline Linux on marble (postmarketOS-style
 U-Boot + extlinux boot), not Android.
 .
 Upstream source: https://github.com/GhfunNiHe/marble-device-support
